---
layout: base.njk
title: SEO Strategist
description: "SEO strategist with 8+ years in technical SEO, local search, and analytics for multi-location healthcare brands. 110+ sites migrated, measurable lead growth."
isHome: true
sitemapPriority: 1.0
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap hero__grid">
    <div>
      <p class="hero__eyebrow">{{ site.tagline }} &middot; {{ site.location.city }}, {{ site.location.regionCode }}</p>
      <h1>SEO strategy that moves the business, not just the rankings.</h1>
      <p class="hero__lede">
        I'm Ben Woodruff. For eight years I've turned complex, multi-location
        healthcare websites into organic acquisition channels &mdash; connecting
        technical SEO, local search, and clean attribution so clients can see
        exactly which work produced the call, the form fill, and the booked
        appointment.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/case-studies/">See the work</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      {% include "partials/hero-photo.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Proof, in numbers</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:var(--space-s)">
      Every figure below is tied to a specific engagement documented on this site.
    </p>
    <ul class="metrics" style="margin-top:var(--space-l)">
      {%- for metric in career.metrics %}
      <li class="metric">
        <p class="metric__value">{{ metric.value }}</p>
        <p class="metric__label">{{ metric.label }}</p>
        <p class="metric__detail">{{ metric.detail }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What I do</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:var(--space-s)">
      Strategy first, then the tactics that actually support it.
    </p>
    <ul class="cards" style="margin-top:var(--space-l)">
      {%- for area in capabilities.areas %}
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="card__title">{{ area.title }}</h3>
        <p class="muted">{{ area.summary }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/capabilities/">Full capability detail</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Selected case studies</h2>
    <ul class="cards" style="margin-top:var(--space-l)">
      {%- for study in collections.caseStudies %}
      <li class="card">
        <p class="card__eyebrow">{{ study.data.discipline }}</p>
        <h3 class="card__title"><a href="{{ study.url }}">{{ study.data.title }}</a></h3>
        <p class="muted">{{ study.data.cardSummary }}</p>
        <p class="card__result">{{ study.data.headlineResult }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <figure class="quote">
      <p>&ldquo;{{ career.testimonial.quote }}&rdquo;</p>
      <figcaption>
        &mdash; {{ career.testimonial.author }}, {{ career.testimonial.role }}
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow stack">
    <h2>Let's talk</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      I'm currently exploring SEO strategist roles where I can own strategy for a
      portfolio of accounts and work alongside content, development, paid media,
      and client-facing teams.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ site.resume }}">Download r&eacute;sum&eacute; (PDF)</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
